From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wireless: add a Kconfig anchor for the out-of-tree Morse driver

The vendor builds the Morse Micro HaLow driver in tree, and its Kconfig
selects CRC7 and the CCMP/GCMP crypto. Built out of tree here, nothing
selects CRC7 (prompt-less), so morse.ko cannot link crc7_be. Add a
symbol that carries those selects.

diff --color -ruN a/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig b/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig	2026-10-18 14:50:59.502725450 -0300
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig	2026-10-18 14:50:59.519733783 -0300
@@ -35,6 +35,21 @@
 source "drivers/net/wireless/st/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/wireless/ti/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/wireless/zydas/Kconfig"
+
+config MORSE_HALOW_DEPS
+	tristate "Kernel support for the out-of-tree Morse Micro HaLow driver"
+	depends on MAC80211
+	select CRC7
+	select CRYPTO_AES
+	select CRYPTO_CCM
+	select CRYPTO_GCM
+	select CRYPTO_CMAC
+	select CRYPTO_CTR
+	help
+	  Selects what the Morse Micro 802.11ah driver (built out of tree, as
+	  the reCamera package morse-driver) needs from the kernel; these are
+	  the selects of the driver's own Kconfig (WLAN_VENDOR_MORSE).  CRC7
+	  has no prompt, so it can only be enabled this way.
 source "drivers/net/wireless/quantenna/Kconfig"
 
 source "drivers/net/wireless/virtual/Kconfig"
